     "source": "s1",
     "quote": "In Greek mythology, Cassandra, also spelled Kassandra or Casandra, (; Ancient Greek: Κασ(σ)άνδρα, pronounced [kas:ándra], or referred to as Alexandra; Ἀλεξάνδρα) was a Trojan priestess dedicated to the god Apollo and fated by him to utter true prophecies, but never to be believed.",
